WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.060
OSINT draws from many public source categories,

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:05.085
each with different strengths and limitations.

00:00:05.085 --> 00:00:08.615
Search engines help discover material, but their results are ranked, incomplete,

00:00:08.615 --> 00:00:10.440
personalized, and subject to change.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:14.455
Analysts should treat search results as discovery aids rather than evidence by themselves.

00:00:14.455 --> 00:00:18.875
Websites and official public records can provide direct statements, filings, policies,

00:00:18.875 --> 00:00:20.600
notices, and historical context.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:24.460
News organizations and specialist publications may add reporting and expert

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:25.311
interpretation.

00:00:25.311 --> 00:00:30.040
Forums and social platforms can surface early observations, but identity, authenticity,

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:32.915
motive, and context often require careful validation.

00:00:32.915 --> 00:00:37.170
Domain and DNS data can help describe public-facing infrastructure and relationships at a

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.455
point in time.

00:00:38.455 --> 00:00:42.680
Code repositories may expose public project history, dependencies, documentation,

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:44.485
or security advisories.

00:00:44.485 --> 00:00:48.235
Collection must remain within lawful public access and organizational policy;

00:00:48.235 --> 00:00:52.195
public-source work never authorizes access to private repositories or accounts.

00:00:52.195 --> 00:00:56.980
Images and video may contain visible objects, text, landmarks, weather, shadows, edits,

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:58.255
or publication metadata.

00:00:58.255 --> 00:01:01.620
Maps and geospatial sources can help test location claims.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:05.815
Visual analysis should avoid identifying or tracking private individuals without lawful

00:01:05.815 --> 00:01:07.010
authority and a legitimate,

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:08.395
proportionate purpose.

00:01:08.395 --> 00:01:10.375
Source selection should follow the requirement.

00:01:10.375 --> 00:01:12.475
Official records may be strong for a legal filing,

00:01:12.475 --> 00:01:15.680
while direct technical documentation may be better for a software behavior.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:19.955
A social post may provide a lead but not enough support for a consequential judgment.

00:01:19.955 --> 00:01:24.420
Maintain a source inventory that records ownership, access conditions, update patterns,

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:26.580
expected reliability, and preservation needs.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:27.930
Diversity matters:

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:31.845
independent sources with different origins provide stronger corroboration than many sites

00:01:31.845 --> 00:01:33.160
repeating the same original claim.
